---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import ProgressDemo from "../../components/ProgressDemo";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Progress"
  description="A thin bar that shows how far a task has come, or that it is still waiting."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Progress</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Shows how much of a task is done, such as an upload or storage that fills
    up. When the amount is not known yet, pass <code>null</code> and the bar slides.
    For a short wait with no amount, use Spinner.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><ProgressDemo client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Progress usage"
      code={`import {
  Progress,
  ProgressLabel,
  ProgressValue,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/progress";

<Progress value={40}>
  <ProgressLabel>Progress</ProgressLabel>
  <ProgressValue />
</Progress>

<Progress value={null}>
  <ProgressLabel>Waiting</ProgressLabel>
  <ProgressValue />
</Progress>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>Progress</code> renders the track and indicator for you. Its children
      sit on one row above the track: <code>ProgressLabel</code> at the start and
      <code>ProgressValue</code> at the end. The row gap is 8px and the track is 4px
      tall.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>value</code>: a number from <code>min</code> to
        <code>max</code> (0–100 by default), or <code>null</code> when the amount
        is unknown.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>format</code> and <code>locale</code> change how the value is written.
        <code>ProgressValue</code> also takes a function child.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>ProgressTrack</code> and <code>ProgressIndicator</code> are the parts
        <code>Progress</code> uses. Use them only to build your own bar.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Every part takes <code>className</code> (a string or a function of the state)
      and a Base UI <code>render</code> prop. The root, track, indicator, label, and
      value get <code>data-progressing</code>,
      <code>data-complete</code>, or <code>data-indeterminate</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Bare bar</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Name it with aria-label and read sizes"
      code={`<Progress value={Math.min(100, percent)} aria-label="Workspace storage used" />

<Progress
  value={Math.floor((sent / size) * 100)}
  aria-label={\`Uploading \${name}\`}
  getAriaValueText={() => \`Uploading \${formatFileSize(sent)} of \${formatFileSize(size)}\`}
/>`}
    />
    <p>
      With no children, the bar stands alone. Keep the real numbers in text next
      to it, and name it with <code>aria-label</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The root is a <code>progressbar</code> with <code>aria-valuemin</code>,
      <code>aria-valuemax</code>, and <code>aria-valuenow</code>. A
      <code>ProgressLabel</code> names it; otherwise pass
      <code>aria-label</code>. <code>getAriaValueText</code> replaces the percent
      that a screen reader reads, for example with “Uploading 3.1 MB of 8.4 MB”. <code
        >ProgressValue</code
      > is hidden from screen readers, because the bar already reads the value.
    </p>
    <p>
      While the value is <code>null</code>, <code>aria-valuenow</code> is left out.
      The width changes in 180ms. With reduced motion, the width jumps and the sliding
      bar becomes a faint full track.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      The track uses <code>--sprout-secondary</code> and the indicator
      <code>--sprout-primary</code>, so the bar takes the brand color in the
      TulipFarm theme. The label uses <code>--sprout-text</code> and the value
      <code>--sprout-muted</code>. In forced colors, the indicator is
      <code>Highlight</code> on an outlined track.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
